China region selection reference
===============================

The unmodified catalog.json is dist/pca-code.json from
modood/Administrative-divisions-of-China, pinned to repository commit
c49d495b40ac73eb1a66f6eeae5f8fd10696f035 (2025-12-27).
The data file was last changed at dc3a1d7acd85ca1b0979543e9259604142c52e8e
(2023-09-13). Upstream licenses this repository under WTFPL Version 2;
the original license is preserved verbatim in LICENSE.

https://github.com/modood/Administrative-divisions-of-China

Upstream describes the data as the 2023 National Bureau of Statistics
statistical division snapshot, as of 2023-06-30, published 2023-09-11.
Its pinned README says that the project is no longer updated and that the
statistics bureau stopped publishing the individual codes in October 2024.
This is a historical selection reference, not a statement of current legal
administrative divisions or proof of current job coverage.

Coverage: 31 mainland province-level units, 342 prefecture-level nodes
(including statistical grouping nodes), and 3,056 third-level entries.
Hong Kong (HK), Macao (MO), and Taiwan (TW) are absent from this source.
The UI separately offers these three existing domestic-market country/region
codes as region-only choices, labeled as having no subordinate catalog.
Their map selection keys CN-HK/CN-MO/CN-TW reuse the existing Natural Earth
display grouping. No cities, districts, county codes or coordinates are
invented for them. These three choices are not entries in catalog.json.

Of the third-level entries, 2,974 have six-digit statistical codes, including
some development/management areas, and 82 have nine-digit township codes.
Dongguan, Zhongshan, Danzhou and Jiayuguan directly list towns, streets or
functional areas in the upstream third slot. The UI must not label these
as legally constituted districts or counties. Municipality "市辖区"/"县"
and province-administered county-level groups retain their original codes
and names; a display label may add their parent municipality for clarity.

BetterMe uses this file only for province/city/district selection and literal
matching against already disclosed location text. Catalog membership does
not establish an employer location, job administrative fields, coordinates,
office precision, or current availability. No location facts are added to
jobs and no map coordinates are derived from this directory. Ambiguous short
city names are omitted from automatic text aliases; unknown locations remain
unknown. The shared query still requires country and all selected levels on
the same disclosed location.

provinceMapIds in source-manifest.json copies identifiers only from the
existing Natural Earth derived china-provinces-10m.geojson by an exact,
unique Chinese province-name join. Its own source/license notice remains at
apps/web/src/components/atlas/geo/NOTICE.md. This crosswalk is for map/UI
selection and literal identifier matching, not enrichment of job facts.

Pinned URLs, source dates, exact file byte sizes, SHA-256 checksums and
crosswalk provenance are recorded in source-manifest.json.
